{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL Injection vulnerability via cancel_reason","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":51},"explanation":"The cancel_reason string from the request JSON is interpolated directly into the SQL update string instead of being passed as a query parameter. An attacker can supply a malicious string containing SQL commands to manipulate the database.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries for the cancel_reason, e.g., db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":941,"output_tokens":230,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":1,"cached_requests":1,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":0.002,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL Injection vulnerability in cancel_order","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":51},"explanation":"The cancellation reason from the request body is interpolated directly into the SQL query string (sql = f\"...\"). This allows an attacker to perform SQL injection attacks by supplying malicious input in the 'reason' field.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries for the cancel reason: db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":941,"output_tokens":227,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":1,"cached_requests":1,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":0.001,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":2,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL Injection vulnerability in cancel_order","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":51},"explanation":"The cancel_reason from the request JSON is directly interpolated into the SQL string without parameterization or escaping. This allows an attacker to perform SQL injection attacks via the 'reason' field.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries for the cancel_reason, e.g., UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":941,"output_tokens":210,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":1,"cached_requests":0,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":1.474,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Missing check for whether the updated user exists","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":37},"explanation":"The endpoint executes an UPDATE query without checking if any rows were actually affected or if the user exists. If an invalid `user_id` is passed, the database update silently does nothing, but if `notify` is True, `get_user` may return None or raise an error when attempting to access `user.email` on line 37.","suggested_fix":"Check the number of affected rows or verify the user exists before proceeding to send notifications, returning a 404 error if not found.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"none-user","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1035,"output_tokens":245,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":1,"cached_requests":1,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":0.002,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Missing check for whether the updated user exists","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":37},"explanation":"The UPDATE statement executes even if the user_id does not exist, and if notify is true, get_user(db, int(user_id)) will likely return None, causing an AttributeError when accessing user.email.","suggested_fix":"Check if the user exists or check the number of changed rows just like deactivate_user does, raising a 404 error if not found.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"none-user","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1035,"output_tokens":220,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":1,"cached_requests":1,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":0.001,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":2,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Missing check for whether the user exists during role update","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":33},"explanation":"The endpoint executes an SQL UPDATE statement without checking if any rows were affected. If a non-existent user_id is provided, it returns a 204 No Content status and attempts to fetch/email a non-existent user or silently completes without indicating failure.","suggested_fix":"Check the number of changed rows or query the user beforehand, raising an HTTPError(404, \"user not found\") if the user does not exist.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"unvalidated-role","distance":2,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":1035,"output_tokens":233,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":1,"cached_requests":0,"agent":null,"duration_seconds":8.522,"error":null}
